/**
 * Stages N-Triples and N-Quads input on all workers.
 *
 * <p>
 * The coordinator reads the input in line-aligned blocks. A worker parses one block, encodes its terms, routes every
 * statement component and every new value occurrence to its partition, and compresses each partition's share of the
 * block into one frame. The coordinator appends finished frames to the staged partition files strictly in block order,
 * so every staged component file stays in ascending statement order.
 * </p>
 *
 * <p>
 * Statement {@code k} of block {@code b} gets the ordinal {@code (b << 32) | k}. Ordinals therefore follow input order
 * but are not dense; resolution converts them to dense statement numbers when it assembles the ID-quad spool.
 * </p>
 */
